{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>So the daughters of Tzelofchad, etc.</b> It was necessary to say <b>כֵּן</b> ('so'), and it did not suffice to merely spell out the legal rulings — to say that the way of the judgment they rendered with their intellect applies to all the explanations we have given: whether according to what the Tanna said, that they were wise women who derived the law of inheritance from the law of yibum — HaShem vindicated what they judged with their intellect; or according to what they said of their own understanding, that the portions of the firstborn and the portion of their brother pertain to them. Further, HaShem devised to say ״כֵּן״ etc., to signal that all the details of the laws that HaShem would command concerning this matter — as the Sages of blessed memory expounded in the baraita in tractate Bava Batra (118:) — and this is their language: ״נָתֹן תִּתֵּן״ — this is the inheritance of their father; ״בְּתוֹךְ אֲחֵי״ etc. — this is the inheritance of their father's father; ״וְהַעֲבַרְתָּ״ — this is the firstborn portion, etc.; and Rabbi Elazar said: also the portion of their father's brother, etc., as it is written ״נָתֹן תִּתֵּן״ etc. — to all these details the daughters of Tzelofchad intended in their words, and it is what He says: <b>כֵּן בְּנוֹת</b> etc., and He then returned to spell out the things He had included in the statement ״כֵּן.״ From this you learn that their intention was to ask about everything stated, and we have already alluded to them above in their words." "And HaShem also intended to exalt the righteous, wise women, and perhaps it was for this that He intended in the word <b>לֵאמֹר</b> — in the sense of exalting, as in His saying (Deuteronomy 26:18) ״הֶאֱמִירְךָ הַיּוֹם״ — to elevate them through the statement ״כֵּן בְּנוֹת צְלָפְחָד דֹּבְרֹת.״ Further, HaShem intended to give them a separate response to their claim, and not to include them together with Israel in a single commandment as He commanded nearby, where it is written: ״וְאֶל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל תְּדַבֵּר לֵאמֹר״ — to show that He honors those who honor Him and do His will."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:15:31.261526726Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}